Third-party material

This product bundles third-party material under its own licenses, listed below. The per-file
list (author, source, license) is in assets/ATTRIBUTION.md.

Inter (assets/fonts/Inter-*.ttf) — SIL Open Font License 1.1. See assets/fonts/OFL-Inter.txt.
Showcase photographs by Ansel Adams, Dorothea Lange and NASA (docs/images/) — public domain. See assets/ATTRIBUTION.md.

crates/inpaint (lightcraft-inpaint), taken from upstream storytold/lightcraft, ports the inpainting
(PatchMatch completion) and Poisson membrane fill code of PhotoCraft
(https://github.com/storytold/photocraft, crates/algo/src/inpaint.rs and poisson.rs), Copyright the
PhotoCraft contributors, licensed under the MIT License or the Apache License 2.0, at your option.
The port was modified by the LightCraft contributors (2026); each ported file says so.

crates/segment (lightcraft-segment) ports the SAM 3 model code of Hugging Face Transformers
(https://github.com/huggingface/transformers, src/transformers/models/sam3 and sam3_tracker),
Copyright The HuggingFace Team and Meta Platforms, Inc., licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
The port was modified by the LightCraft contributors (2026): translated from Python/PyTorch to
Rust on candle and restructured; each ported file says so. Because of this, crates/segment is
licensed under the Apache License 2.0 only (LICENSE-APACHE), not under the MIT option.

crates/segment/src/segformer.rs ports the SegFormer model of candle-transformers
(https://github.com/huggingface/candle, candle-transformers/src/models/segformer.rs), Copyright
the Candle authors, licensed under the MIT License or the Apache License 2.0, itself a port of
Hugging Face Transformers (src/transformers/models/segformer, Apache License 2.0). The port was
modified by the LightCraft contributors (2026); the file says how. The SegFormer weights it runs
(nvidia/segformer-b5-finetuned-ade-640-640, sayeed99/segformer_b3_clothes,
jonathandinu/face-parsing) are not part of LightCraft: a user downloads them only when they choose
to, under each checkpoint's own terms (see docs/ai-masks.md).
patches/egui-wgpu is egui-wgpu 0.36.2 (https://github.com/emilk/egui, crates/egui-wgpu), Copyright
the egui authors, licensed under the MIT License or the Apache License 2.0, at your option. It is
used through [patch.crates-io] and was modified by the LightCraft contributors (2026) so the window
can be an HDR (EDR) half-float surface; every change is marked "LightCraft patch".
Camera Raw-matched operators in crates/pipeline (Bryan's fork, round 10: texture_cr.rs,
grading_cr.rs with grading_cr.bin, bw_cr.rs with bw_cr.bin, point_color_cr.rs) are ported from
RAWmakase (https://github.com/pch/rawmakase, crates/rawmakase-engine/src/develop: texture.rs,
laplacian.rs, color_grade_curves.rs and color_grade_curves.bin, black_white.rs and
black_white_chart.bin, color_mixer.rs, point_color.rs), Copyright (c) 2026 RAWmakase
contributors, licensed under the MIT License. The tables are RAWmakase's measurements of Camera
Raw's output on synthetic charts (no Adobe data). The port was modified by the LightCraft
contributors (2026); each ported file says so.
Round 11 (scene_cr.rs, with scene_cr_rule_data.rs, scene_cr_rule_ext.rs and scene_cr_rule_pair.rs
copied verbatim) ports RAWmakase's scene tone map from the same crate: local_tone.rs (measurement
map, guided base, grid sampling), clarity.rs and clarity_data.rs, scene_tone/haze.rs,
local_tone_rule.rs and local_tone_rule_data.rs, local_tone_rule_ext_data.rs,
local_tone_rule_pair_data.rs (fitted networks and tables), under the same MIT License.

